Title: F2-M10 — No Flags at Dawn (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. FOUNDRY GALLERY, BLACK BASIN FORWARD BASE - BEFORE DAWN

[[AMBIENCE: wind in iron rafters, furnace slag cooling, vehicles forming up below]]
[[MUSIC: low, resolute tension building]]

A captured plan of the coordination hub is spread across a foundry bench. COMMANDER SAVA and LENKA stand over it. Lenka's sleeve of files is thicker than it has ever been.

LENKA
(determined)
Both armies received forged orders from this hub. The evidence vault contains the original transmission keys.

COMMANDER SAVA
(measured)
Its defence system has no flag recognition. It will fire on whoever enters.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: player base in the east, hub wall with three entrances, evidence vault at the centre, control bunker inside the ring unmarked, culvert on the south-west perimeter, west boundary where the Meridian column will cross]]

LENKA
The blueprints from the Iron Choir described guns without crews. The hub wall is on the plan. The guns are not. I take that as a warning, not an absence.

COMMANDER SAVA
(clipped)
The risks, in order. The guns we cannot see. A Meridian column due on the west boundary in twelve minutes, coming for the same vault. And a hub that was built by people who planned for being found.

LENKA
We need the vault whole. Not rubble. Rubble tells both governments what they already believe.

COMMANDER SAVA
(serious)
Scouts out first. Engineers behind them. If there is a quiet way into that ring, I want it before the siege guns start.

LENKA
(firm)
Secure the vault and disable the automated guns. We need the evidence intact, and we need it before the hub self-destructs.

COMMANDER SAVA
(quieter)
Command gave me an order this morning. I have not read it yet. Whatever is in that vault, Lenka, we read it first.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
